1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,230
Hello?

2
00:00:03,230 --> 00:00:09,080
Oh, hello. I wanted to enquire about hiring a room in the Village Hall

3
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:11,800
for the evening of September the first.

4
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:18,600
Let me just see... Yes, we have both rooms available that evening.

5
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:24,180
There's our Main Hall - that's got seating for 200 people

6
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:26,400
Or there's the Charlton Room...

7
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,550
Sorry?

8
00:00:27,550 --> 00:00:34,970
The Charlton Room - C-H-A-R-L-T-O-N.

9
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:38,150
That's got seating for up to one hundred.

10
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:43,290
Well, we're organizing a dinner to raise money for a charity,

11
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:46,980
and we're hoping for at least 150 people

12
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,570
so I think well go for the Main Hall. How much would that cost?

13
00:00:53,570 --> 00:00:59,010
Let's see. You wanted it for the evening of September 1st?

14
00:00:59,010 --> 00:01:01,070
Yes, that's a Saturday.

15
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:06,960
So from six pm to midnight that'd be 115

16
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:13,370
that's the weekend price, it's 75 on weekdays.

17
00:01:13,370 --> 00:01:15,000
That's all right.

18
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,139
And I have to tell you there's also a deposit of 250,

19
00:01:20,139 --> 00:01:24,850
which is returnable of course as long as there's no damage.

20
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:31,220
But we do insist that this is paid in cash, we don't take cards for that.

21
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:35,960
You can pay the actual rent of the room however you like

22
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:39,230
though - cash, credit card, cheque...

23
00:01:39,230 --> 00:01:41,850
Oh, well I suppose that's OK.

24
00:01:41,850 --> 00:01:47,650
So does the charge include use of tables and chairs and so on?

25
00:01:47,650 --> 00:01:48,750
Oh, yes.

26
00:01:48,750 --> 00:01:51,400
And what about parking?

27
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:57,560
Yeah, that's all included. The only thing that isn't included is

28
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:59,870
you said you were organising a dinner?

29
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:00,560
Yeah.

30
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:07,520
Well, you'll have to pay extra for the kitchen if you want to use that. It's 25.

31
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:13,220
It's got very good facilities - good quality cookers and fridges and so on.

32
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:20,010
OK, well I suppose that's all right. We can cover the cost in our entry charges.

33
00:02:20,010 --> 00:02:23,070
Right. So I'll make a note of that.

34
00:02:23,070 --> 00:02:29,450
Now there are just one or two things you need to think about before the event.

35
00:02:29,450 --> 00:02:33,300
For example, you'll have to see about getting a licence

36
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:36,660
if you're planning to have any music during the meal.

37
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:37,720
Oh, really?

38
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:41,950
It's quite straightforward, I'll give you the details later on.

39
00:02:41,950 --> 00:02:48,910
And about a week or ten days before your event you'll need to contact the caretaker,

40
00:02:48,910 --> 00:02:55,000
that's Mr Evans, to make the arrangements for entry. He'll sort that out with you.

41
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,100
And do I give him the payment as well?

42
00:02:58,100 --> 00:03:00,850
No, you do that directly with me.

43
00:03:00,850 --> 00:03:10,400
Right. Now is there anything I need to know about what happens during the event?

44
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:16,090
Well, as you'll be aware, of course the building is no smoking throughout.

45
00:03:16,090 --> 00:03:17,170
Of course.

46
00:03:17,170 --> 00:03:19,280
Now, are you having a band?

47
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:20,510
Yes.

48
00:03:20,510 --> 00:03:22,982
Well, they'll have a lot of equipment,

49
00:03:22,982 --> 00:03:28,400
so rather than using the front door they should park their van round the back

50
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:30,400
and use the stage door there.

51
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:35,330
You can open that from inside but don't forget to lock it at the end.

52
00:03:35,330 --> 00:03:36,370
OK.

53
00:03:36,370 --> 00:03:40,760
And talking of bands, I'm sure I don't need to tell you this

54
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:44,851
but you must make sure that no one fiddles about

55
00:03:44,851 --> 00:03:49,551
with the black box by the fire door that's a system that cuts in

56
00:03:49,591 --> 00:03:54,070
when the volume reaches a certain level. It's a legal requirement

57
00:03:54,070 --> 00:03:58,540
Sure. Anyway, we want people to be able to talk to one another

58
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:01,050
so we don't want anything too loud.

59
00:04:01,050 --> 00:04:08,380
Oh, that reminds me, we'll be having speeches - are there any microphones available?

60
00:04:08,380 --> 00:04:12,570
Yeah. Just let the caretaker know, he'll get those for you.

61
00:04:12,570 --> 00:04:19,710
Right, now when the event is over we do ask that the premises are left in good condition.

62
00:04:19,710 --> 00:04:22,060
So there's a locked cupboard

63
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:26,250
and you'll be informed of the code you need to open that.

64
00:04:26,250 --> 00:04:32,000
It's got all the cleaning equipment, brushes and detergent and so on.

65
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:39,440
Right. So what do we need to do after everyone's gone? Sweep the floors I suppose?

66
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:43,700
Well, actually they have to be washed, not just swept.

67
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:46,938
Then you'll be provided with black plastic bags,

68
00:04:46,938 --> 00:04:52,200
so all the rubbish must be collected up and left outside the door.

69
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:56,100
Of course. We'll make sure everything's left tidy.

70
00:04:56,100 --> 00:05:02,340
Oh, and I forgot to ask, I presume we can have decorations in the room?

71
00:05:02,340 --> 00:05:05,820
Yes, but you must take them down afterwards.

72
00:05:05,820 --> 00:05:06,720
Sure.

73
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:12,260
And the chairs and tables should be stacked up neatly at the back of the room.

74
00:05:12,260 --> 00:05:17,000
I'll make sure I've got a few people to help me.
